DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't react to intraday panic.</b> The S&P was down 3.2% Wednesday morning and closed down just 0.25%. Keep your regular monthly investing (DCA) rather than selling into a plunge or chasing a rebound.",
"<b>Expect more Fed hikes, not cuts.</b> Core inflation rose to 3.3% and growth is strong (4.3%); a December hike is ~98% priced and markets see two more in total. Plan around higher rates for longer.",
"<b>Fear is extreme, so avoid panic selling.</b> CNN Fear & Greed is 15 and NYSE new lows (259) swamp new highs (33). Extreme fear has often come before recoveries, but timing is unknowable: DCA spreads the risk.",
"<b>Check your AI and chip exposure.</b> The Nasdaq 100 briefly hit bear-market territory and Nvidia fell another 3.9%. If one theme is a big slice of your portfolio, trim back to your target mix.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds still pay.</b> 2-year Treasuries yield ~4.65% and Fed hikes keep savings rates high; that money earns while you wait.",
"<b>Plan for higher loan rates.</b> Another Fed hike looks near-certain on 9 Dec; fix rates where you can and avoid new variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rescue.</b> It briefly fell below $3,500, its lowest in over a year, as rate hikes weigh. Keep it a small slice (e.g. 5-10%) and don't chase daily swings.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> Bitcoin is stuck around $60,000 and trades like a risky tech asset; only invest what you can afford to lose.",
"<b>Thai investors: stay defensive.</b> The SET is at an 8-month low and the US proposed up to 18% tariffs on Thai goods (not final). Favor solid dividend payers bought near their buy zones, and keep some cash."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 15 (15.2) = Extreme Fear, down from 17.4 at Tuesday's close; 30 a week ago and 17 a month ago. Five of the seven signals read extreme fear; price strength and the VIX read fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~54.1 = Elevated (up from 53.2): the Houthis say they hit Saudi Arabia's biggest refinery, Iran reports another tanker mine fire, and Poland plans a no-fly zone on its Ukraine border."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 2.8 = extreme fear, from 3.0 after Wednesday's small dip."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 27.2 = fear, from 28.4; NYSE had 259 new lows vs 33 highs on Wednesday (Tuesday: 144 vs 31)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 17.2 = extreme fear, from 16.6."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 7.0 = extreme fear, from 8.8: heavy demand for downside protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 34.2 on CNN's 0-100 scale = fear (from 42.9), as the VIX rose to ~28.3 after touching ~35 intraday."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 5.2 = extreme fear, from 4.4, as investors kept buying Treasuries."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 13.2 = extreme fear, from 17.8."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 76 (from 75): Iran's army reports another tanker mine fire in Hormuz and the IRGC chief threatens to push 'enemy forces a considerable depth'."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 49 (from 48): Ukraine hits two Samara refineries and an air base; Poland plans a no-fly zone and floated NATO intercepts of Russian missiles over Ukraine."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 94 (from 92): the Houthis say they struck Ras Tanura and Riyadh, Saudi Arabia hit Hodeidah, and the Houthis claim Jeddah and Jizan."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 11 (unchanged): Moscow says it is open to talks on its terms; no US-Iran talks announced."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 31 (unchanged): no new arms-control talks; Iran still refuses to ship out its 60% uranium."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,183 Wednesday (−0.25%) after being down 3.2% at the low; up ~5% this year."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +0.33% Wednesday to about 50,183 after erasing an 1,100-point drop, its biggest reversal since 2022."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −0.62% Wednesday to about 23,586 after −4.6% at the low; the Nasdaq 100 briefly touched bear-market territory (−20% from its October peak)."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.85% Wednesday (−5bp), its eighth straight daily fall; the 2Y was ~4.65%."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$83.7 at Wednesday's settle (+1.99%) after a Houthi attack on Saudi Arabia's Ras Tanura refinery."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$94.6 at Wednesday's January settle (+3.51%); the February contract settled ~$90.6."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.76/gal (AAA, 26 Nov), down from ~$5.96 a week ago and ~$6.35 a month ago."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,536 Comex December settle Wednesday (−0.73%); spot briefly fell below $3,500, a more-than-one-year low, before recovering to ~$3,575."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$60.2k early Thursday = neutral: +0.7% Wednesday after dipping to ~$57.3k; it trades with tech, not as a haven."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike; a December hike to 4.00-4.25% is ~98% priced for 8-9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~98% for a quarter point in December after Wednesday's PCE data; ~1-in-3 odds of a third hike in this cycle's next leg."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~103.7 Wednesday, little changed."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~159.2; the yen is near the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct; Governor Witai says the BoT aims to keep rates steady to support growth but is data-dependent; 2026 GDP forecast kept at 2.4%; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,428.50 on Wed 25 Nov (−23.15, −1.59%), range 1,427.26-1,447.45, an 8-month low (lowest since 24 Mar); brokers see support down to ~1,400."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿1,180M of Thai stocks on Wed 25 Nov; about −฿11.9B so far in November (our tally of daily SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

